## <summary>Type-enforcement domain for the ai-tools sandbox account that runs a coding agent, and the operator-domain attribute its project grants are written on.</summary>

########################################
## <summary>
##	Make a login domain an operator domain: manage and relabel on the project types, and the layout
##	modules' creation transitions. Membership alone: the domain does not gain an entry into
##	ai_tools_t or a launch permission. The ipp_ prefix is what Fedora's SELinux/IndependentPolicy
##	guideline requires of an interface outside the distribution policy, and the name stays apart
##	from the attribute's because an m4 macro named like the attribute would expand every mention
##	of the attribute in a .te file.
## </summary>
## <param name="domain">
##	<summary>
##	The login domain this host confines its operators to (staff_t, a site-written domain).
##	</summary>
## </param>
#
interface(`ipp_ai_tools_add_operator_domain',`
	gen_require(`
		attribute ai_tools_operator_domain;
	')

	typeattribute $1 ai_tools_operator_domain;
')
